On the first day a suggestion added \+55\.4% \(95% CI \+14\.0% to \+111\.7%\). By day 20 it was \+19\.2% \(95% CI \+2\.9% to \+38\.2%\), and by day 30 \+4\.5% \(95% CI \-11\.0% to \+22\.6%\), no longer distinguishable from zero. The model assumes a straight-line decline, so the exact shape is an approximation; the decline itself is clear (\-1\.3% per day, p = 0\.027) and matches the published finding that the effect started large and faded.

